%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 72a2054a7b2ea8346b8e03ab6c5935fc, type: 3}
  m_Name: Handbook
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LostControl.Config.HandbookContent
  pages:
  - title: Basics
    body: '<b>Your job</b>

      Users send a ticket when their PC has a problem.
      Fix every PC before too many users are lost.


      <b>Connecting</b>

      Click
      a ticket in the list to connect to that PC. Connecting takes a few seconds,
      and you can only work on one PC at a time. Disconnect with the button above
      the list.


      <b>The list goes stale</b>

      While you are connecting
      or connected, the other tickets stop updating: they are dimmed and only show
      what you last saw. When a PC you can''t see takes damage, you hear a beep and
      its ticket flashes red. Disconnect to see every ticket live again.


      <b>Rounds</b>

      Each
      PC is fixed by finishing its minigame, some of them a few times in a row. The
      list and the minigame panel show which round you are on. Finished rounds stay
      finished when you leave.


      <b>Pressure</b>

      While a round is unsolved,
      the PC''s pressure meter fills, also while you are working on another PC. When
      it is full, the PC takes damage and the meter drops back to half. Finishing
      a round empties it.


      <b>Damage</b>

      Fine, Slightly broken, More
      broken, Blackout. At Blackout the user is lost and the ticket closes. The level
      ends when every ticket is closed, or when too many users are lost (see Game
      data).'
  - title: Find the off-folder
    body: 'One folder in the grid looks slightly different from the others. Click
      it to finish the round.


      <b>What can be different</b>

      The file
      on the folder, the side of the tab, a small tilt, or the size. In each round
      only one of these is different.


      <b>Careful</b>

      Clicking a folder
      that is not the different one adds pressure.


      <b>Pressure</b>

      The
      meter fills at a steady speed while the round is unsolved.'
  - title: Match the colors
    body: 'All cards start face down, and every colour is on exactly two cards. Click
      a card to see its colour, then click the card with the same colour. Match every
      pair to fix the PC.


      <b>Match</b>

      Both cards stay face up, and
      the pressure meter drops.


      <b>No match</b>

      Both cards show for
      a moment, then turn face down again. A wrong pair costs nothing extra.


      <b>Leaving</b>

      Matched
      pairs stay when you leave this PC. A card you picked but did not match turns
      face down again.


      <b>Pressure</b>

      The meter fills at a steady
      speed until every pair is matched. Each match pushes it back down.'
